  "assumptions": [
    "All cohort sizes, bitrate demands, phase timings, target capacities and deadlines are synthetic, not operator subscriber data or HAPS platform capabilities.",
    "Admission is partial by individual user and sorted by lower priority_rank first, then cohort_id ascending. User-equivalent capacity and aggregate bitrate are hard limits.",
    "No target admission occurs unless target availability and backhaul are true and initiation/preparation/stale-context gates succeed.",
    "Source authority remains active for every user not committed at the target; target authority applies only to users with a completed acknowledged handover. The two authority sets are disjoint.",
    "For a lost completion acknowledgement, admitted users remain unresolved and source-authoritative. Reconciliation is required; target authority is not inferred.",
    "Safety-critical users who are not completed invoke drone_local_safe_mode. This conservative fallback is exercised even when the source path remains the retained authority.",
    "A cohort is homogeneous in declared per-user bitrate and deadline; no RF propagation, interference, mobility, packet queueing or subscriber-level trace is modelled.",
    "Phase durations are deterministic timing inputs, not semi-Markov sojourn-time distributions.",
    "A duplicate completion acknowledgement is ignored idempotently after the first commit; it cannot create extra committed users or a second authority.",
    "This fixture is a protocol-accounting oracle, not a live handover or end-to-end customer SLA result."
